/target

# Cargo.lock IS committed (issue #66). This crate ships a binary
# (`[[bin]] automatised-pipeline`), and for an end product Cargo's own
# guidance is to commit the lock. Ignoring it meant release builds re-resolved
# dependencies on every run, so:
#   - the build was NOT reproducible even with a pinned compiler,
#   - `cargo audit` scanned a lock that never shipped,
#   - the SBOM would have described versions no release was ever built from.
# All three are load-bearing claims of the supply-chain work; none of them
# survive an ignored lockfile.
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/session-cache.json
# Agent worktrees (agent:spawn / Agent isolation). These are checkouts of this
# same repo created for parallel work; committing them would nest the repo
# inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/
benches/runs/

# Python bytecode — scripts/ carries the stdlib-only pin gate and its tests;
# running them locally emits __pycache__ into a repo that is otherwise Rust.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# cargo-mutants output (local mutation runs, not committed)
mutants.out*/
mutants.out*.log

# actionlint is a developer tool installed locally (brew/go install), never
# committed: a tracked 5.8 MB executable is what Scorecard's Binary-Artifacts
# check flags, because a checked-in binary cannot be reviewed and nobody can
# prove it matches upstream.
/actionlint

# cargo-fuzz build output, generated corpora and crash reproducers.
# A corpus is machine-generated search state, not source; crash artifacts are
# attached to their failing CI run and reproduced locally on demand.
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/**
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/
# Exception (issue #148): a few hand-curated libFuzzer artifacts are committed as
# PERMANENT regression seeds — source, not generated search state — so the
# scheduled runs replay them at startup and can never lose the inputs that
# surfaced the failure: the two `parse_file_utf8` artifacts from the OOM report,
# and the `parse_file` input that reproduces the deep-recursion crash the depth
# guard fixes. Everything else under fuzz/corpus/ stays ignored; only these named
# files (and the directories on their path) are tracked.
!fuzz/corpus/
!fuzz/corpus/parse_file_utf8/
!fuzz/corpus/parse_file_utf8/1a9ad06029faf8a98fc125dac137a01def004380
!fuzz/corpus/parse_file_utf8/ae4da5a379eebe86c21aaeb63e0e01c1659472db
!fuzz/corpus/parse_file/
!fuzz/corpus/parse_file/2f76b08c2590a629c2fcbc8839a19e92e2bfc143
